  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></math> denote the complex conjugate of a complex number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> is a non-zero complex number for which both real and imaginary parts of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math> are integers, then which of the following is/are possible value(s) of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>z</mi></mfenced></math> ?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>43</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>205</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>33</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>65</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>13</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>.</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>b</mi></math> (say), given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>Z</mi></math></p><p>Now taking mod both side and squaring we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now comparing from option we get, for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn></math>&nbsp;(i.e <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>We get <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>43</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>205</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}